    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d806">

                <pb facs="1413" n="1366" xml:id="pg1366"/>

                <head>806. Telegram 1193 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d806-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1957-05-14">May 14, 1957, 5:55
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d806-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d806-1"/>
                <p>1193. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>Supplementary guidance regarding paragraph 3 Department’s telegram 1181.</p>
                <p>Public policy on MATADOR deployment to Taiwan has been to emphasize defensive
                    nature of move and treat weapon on same basis as any other piece standard US Air
                    Force equipment. You should take same line, emphasizing need for US defensive
                    arrangements in Taiwan area, but avoiding discussion of propriety this
                    particular weapon if Wang should attempt
                    draw you into discussing this.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
